karadoc wrote:
>
> ... but the problem for gameplay is that since we
> have a limited number of skill slots to use, the lesser weapon types
> get completely shunned. For example, advancing in short swords is just
> a trap. It's essentially just a waste of skill points on a weapon type
> that has no future.

The game has an assortment of "DevTeam traps" that tempted new players
into wasting limited resources.  If you think DevTeam traps are a part
of the game then it makes sense to have weapons that senior players
never use.

> Here are some of the related skill pairs I have in mind.
> dagger & knife

Making crysknife powerful again.  Check.

> spear & javelin

Without an artifact spear this seems pointless.

> dart & shuriken

Multifire shuriken turns into a DevTeam trap.  There is no source for
new ones.

> short sword & long sword

Since long sword is not rare I wonder at this.  In how many games have I
ever gotten a short sword before a long sword?

> scimitar & saber

This would make a common weapon useful.  Check.

> polearm & lance ?

I wonder at why these aren't together as it is.

> bow & crossbow & sling ?

I have thought in terms of making "missile combat" it's own skill.  Sort
of like BanMido's post but he didn't list it in terms of separation of
melee and missile.

> axe & pickaxe ?

Making Cleaver even more confusing?  Fun.


